Landau-Lifshitz-Bloch spin dynamics (fix nve/spin/llb)
======================================================

  in.spin.llb   fcc cobalt with spin magnitudes that relax and fluctuate:
                fix landau/spin gives the magnitudes an energy, and
                fix langevin/spin/llb thermostats the spin directions and
                magnitudes at 300 K.  fix nve/spin/llb integrates the
                spins with the predictor-corrector scheme and the atoms
                with velocity Verlet.  c_savg is the average spin
                magnitude.

The input requires the SPIN and MANYBODY packages and uses the Co potential
of the cobalt_fcc example.  Run it from this directory:

  lmp -in in.spin.llb

Each process draws its own random numbers, so the logs for 1 and 4
processes differ.
